From d26193b1a50471e7df1c11ac4b2c912ac9af1c13 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rust-playground <rp@localhost>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 19:37:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] Run proc macros out of process on Emscripten hosts

rustc compiled to Emscripten cannot dlopen proc-macro crates. Instead, a
proc-macro crate built for Emscripten is compiled to an object and
metadata, and the host links it into a WebAssembly module of its own.
The 'dylib' that dependents load is the crate's metadata; its clients are
trampolines that hand the bridge's buffers to the host, which runs the
macro elsewhere and calls back into rustc for each bridge request.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
